Adaptations:
- Separate PID kref and IPC count fields; preserve 5.10 namespace lifecycle.
- SysV, POSIX queues and native offset-based IPC sysctl handlers.
- Validate anonymous classic-CFI callback jump tables by their branch targets.
- Use temporary fixmap aliases for native rodata tables, as the 5.10 instruction
  patch helper only supports kernel text and module vmalloc addresses.
- Two native BPF iterator callback pairs; this baseline lacks task_vma iteration
  and runtime BTF needed for userspace tracing-program loading.
- Preserve native FUSE initialization and release PID references in fuse_free_conn.
- No native memfd namespace policy or pidfd namespace ioctl; SHM_HUGETLB and
  32-bit IPC are not supported.
- Reference BTF is generated from DDK DWARF. If runtime BTF is unavailable,
  automatic loading requires the exact validated kernel notes/build fingerprint.
